subject: test(usage): lock DefaultExecutor stream_options injection — BUG-OR-01

Regression coverage for the OpenRouter usage-tracking bug: the generic
DefaultExecutor never injected stream_options:{include_usage:true}, so
streaming OpenRouter responses carried no usage object and the gateway
fell back to a characters/4 estimate (dropping usage entirely for
tool-only / empty-text responses).

The fix itself landed in 6754d9c0 (transformRequest now takes  +
 and injects behind supportsIncludeUsage()). This test locks
the gate matrix so it cannot regress:
- injects for streaming chat-completions (openrouter, format=openai)
- no injection non-streaming, no-messages, or non-openai formats
- never clobbers a caller-supplied stream_options
- openai-compatible-<chat> yes / <responses> no
- quirks.noIncludeUsage opt-out honored

Evidence: 8/8 pass; full v3 suite 2683 passed / 75 failed vs policy
baseline 2657/76 (no new failures).

